{"ClientSettings":{"Pn":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"P"},"Sc":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"H"},"Qz":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"T"},"Ap":true,"Mute":true,"Lad":"2026-09-05T00:00:00Z","Iotd":0,"Gwb":0,"Tns":0,"Dft":null,"Mvs":0,"Flt":0,"Imp":1,"Tobn":0},"MediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"A day at the beach is rarely quiet when California sea lions are around. With their booming barks, playful personalities and a knack for stealing the spotlight, these marine mammals know how to put on a show.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.SardineBait_EN-GB5662354179_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.SardineBait_EN-GB5662354179_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Masters of the surf and shore","Title":"California sea lions hunting a sardine bait ball, offshore Mexico, Pacific Ocean","Copyright":"© Henley Spiers/Nature Picture Library","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"California sea lions can dive as deep as 300 metres and hold their breath for up to 10 minutes.","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260905_SardineBait\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=California+sea+lion&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260904_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260905_SardineBait"},"Ssd":"20260905","Name":"SardineBait","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"5662354179","FullDateString":"5 Sept 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Rising above the salt marshes along Germany's North Sea coast, Westerheversand Lighthouse is instantly recognisable for its distinctive red-and-white stripes. Built between 1906 and 1908 on 127 heavy wooden piles driven into the sand, the 40-metre cast-iron tower has stood on the Eiderstedt Peninsula for more than a century, guiding ships through the North Sea. Two identical white keeper's cottages flank the beacon, adding to its storybook appearance.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.Westerheversand_EN-GB5592839708_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.Westerheversand_EN-GB5592839708_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Red and white on the horizon","Title":"Westerheversand Lighthouse in Westerhever, Schleswig-Holstein, Germany","Copyright":"© bluejayphoto/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/54.373402,8.6399/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=54.373402,8.6399;S9;Westerheversand Lighthouse, Schleswig-Holstein, Germany&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260904_Westerheversand\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Westerheversand+Lighthouse&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260903_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260904_Westerheversand"},"Ssd":"20260904","Name":"Westerheversand","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"5592839708","FullDateString":"4 Sept 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Waves usually belong to the ocean. In northern Arizona, United States, they rise from the desert instead. The swirling sandstone formations of Coyote Buttes, part of Vermilion Cliffs National Monument, were shaped by ancient dunes and millions of years of erosion, creating a landscape that seems to ripple even while standing still.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.AZWilderness_EN-GB2345947468_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.AZWilderness_EN-GB2345947468_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"An act of wilderness","Title":"Coyote Buttes, Vermilion Cliffs National Monument, Arizona, United States","Copyright":"© James Hager/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/36.7783,-111.7361/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=36.7783,-111.7361;S9;Vermilion Cliffs National Monument, Arizona, United States&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260903_AZWilderness\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Wilderness+Act+of+1964&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260902_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260903_AZWilderness"},"Ssd":"20260903","Name":"AZWilderness","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"2345947468","FullDateString":"3 Sept 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Along England's east coast, the Suffolk Heritage Coast blends windswept heaths, marshes, shingle beaches and expansive North Sea views. One of its best-known towns is Southwold, where water and history are inseparable. Almost encircled by the sea, the River Blyth and surrounding wetlands, the town occupies a slender peninsula shaped by centuries of fishing, trade and life at the edge of the water.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.SuffolkHuts_EN-GB2261622731_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.SuffolkHuts_EN-GB2261622731_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Painted along the shore","Title":"Traditional beach huts, Southwold, Suffolk Heritage Coast, England","Copyright":"© stevendocwra/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/52.326221,1.678968/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=52.326221,1.678968;S9;Southwold, Suffolk, England&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260902_SuffolkHuts\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Southwold+Suffolk&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260901_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260902_SuffolkHuts"},"Ssd":"20260902","Name":"SuffolkHuts","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"2261622731","FullDateString":"2 Sept 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Tiny mushrooms often go unnoticed, but the horsehair parachute fungus deserves a closer look. With a stem as thin as a strand of horsehair and a pleated cap measuring just 0.5 to 1 centimetre across, this miniature mushroom proves that good things really do come in small packages.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.HorseHairShroom_EN-GB2103309829_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.HorseHairShroom_EN-GB2103309829_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"A world beneath your feet","Title":"Horsehair parachute fungus, Belarus","Copyright":"© Máté/Nature Picture Library","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"Even after drying into a seemingly lifeless speck during drought, the horsehair parachute fungus springs back to life within hours of rainfall, ready to release its spores.","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260901_HorseHairShroom\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Horsehair+parachute+fungus&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260831_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260901_HorseHairShroom"},"Ssd":"20260901","Name":"HorseHairShroom","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"2103309829","FullDateString":"1 Sept 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Stand in Registan Square and it's easy to see why it is considered the architectural heart of Samarkand—one of Central Asia's oldest cities. This plaza in Uzbekistan is framed by three magnificent madrasas—Islamic centres of learning—whose soaring portals draw the eye upwards. Yet some of the square's greatest treasures reveal themselves only when you look closer.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.SamarkandCeiling_EN-GB2027090405_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.SamarkandCeiling_EN-GB2027090405_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"A master class in pattern","Title":"Building detail of Registan Square, Samarkand, Uzbekistan","Copyright":"© Piero M. Bianchi/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/39.655009,66.975755/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=39.655009,66.975755;S9;Registan Square, Samarkand, Uzbekistan&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260831_SamarkandCeiling\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Samarkand&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260830_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260831_SamarkandCeiling"},"Ssd":"20260831","Name":"SamarkandCeiling","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"2027090405","FullDateString":"31 Aug 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Today, International Whale Shark Day makes room for the world's largest fish. Despite their name, whale sharks are not whales but fish, reaching lengths of up to 18 metres and weighing around 18 tonnes. Found in warm tropical seas, they glide through the water with their mouths open, filtering plankton, fish eggs and other tiny prey. This species' distinctive white-spot patterns are unique to each individual, much like human fingerprints.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.YellowShark_EN-GB1905405727_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.YellowShark_EN-GB1905405727_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"The fish that outgrew its name","Title":"Whale shark and golden trevally, Cenderawasih Bay, West Papua, Indonesia","Copyright":"© Pete Oxford/Nature Picture Library","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"Whale sharks may live for a century or more, giving the world's largest fish an unexpectedly long life span.","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260830_YellowShark\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Whale+shark&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260829_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260830_YellowShark"},"Ssd":"20260830","Name":"YellowShark","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"1905405727","FullDateString":"30 Aug 2026"}],"PreloadMediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"What happens when a grand classical concert lets its hair down? The Last Night of the Proms. The finale of the annual BBC Proms turns London's Royal Albert Hall into a joyful, flag-waving party, where world-class music meets quirky costumes, inflatable toys and enthusiastic singalongs.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.LastNightOfTheProms2026_EN-GB7492486139_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.LastNightOfTheProms2026_EN-GB7492486139_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"A finale worth singing about","Title":"Interior of the Royal Albert Hall, London","Copyright":"© William Barton/Shutterstock","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/51.500916,-0.177366/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=51.500916,-0.177366;S9;Royal Albert Hall, London, England&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260912_LastNightOfTheProms2026\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Night+of+the+Proms+London&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260911_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260912_LastNightOfTheProms2026"},"Ssd":"20260912","Name":"LastNightOfTheProms2026","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"7492486139","FullDateString":"12 Sept 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"In September, the French Riviera is bathed in softer light, and the Mediterranean vegetation begins to regain its vibrancy. Along the coast, rosemary, wild thyme and Aleppo pine scent the air, while sailboats drift across the sheltered waters of Villefranche-sur-Mer.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.FrenchRivieraVillage_EN-GB7299831823_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.FrenchRivieraVillage_EN-GB7299831823_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Where the Mediterranean reigns supreme","Title":"The bay of Villefranche-sur-Mer, Alpes-Maritimes, Provence-Alpes-Côte d'Azur, France","Copyright":"© StockByM/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/43.703599,7.312096/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=43.703599,7.312096;S9;Provence-Alpes-Côte d'Azur, France&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260911_FrenchRivieraVillage\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Villefranche-sur-Mer&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260910_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260911_FrenchRivieraVillage"},"Ssd":"20260911","Name":"FrenchRivieraVillage","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"7299831823","FullDateString":"11 Sept 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Ever wondered why Andalusia is one of Spain's best-known regions? Flamenco, tapas, Moorish architecture and extensive olive groves all play a part. Beyond its famous cities, you'll find historic places like Olvera. Surrounded by more than 2 million olive trees, this village developed as a strategic frontier settlement shaped by centuries of change. The Castle of Olvera still watches over the town, while the Church of Our Lady of the Incarnation dominates the skyline below. Visit La Cilla Cultural Center to discover Olvera's medieval history and traditions.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.Olvera_EN-GB6934313279_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.Olvera_EN-GB6934313279_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"A patchwork from above","Title":"Aerial view of Olvera, Andalusia, Spain","Copyright":"© Marco Bottigelli/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/36.935253,-5.267688/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=36.935253,-5.267688;S9;Olvera, Andalusia, Spain&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260910_Olvera\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Olvera+Andalusia+Spain&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260909_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260910_Olvera"},"Ssd":"20260910","Name":"Olvera","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"6934313279","FullDateString":"10 Sept 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"When people think of South India, they often picture spice routes, classical music, folk traditions and a coastline shaped by centuries of maritime life. Follow Karnataka's Arabian Sea coast to the quieter shores of Gabit Keni Beach near Ankola, where fishing remains part of everyday life.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.GabitKeni_EN-GB6382808847_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.GabitKeni_EN-GB6382808847_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Life on India's west coast","Title":"Gabit Keni Beach near Ankola, Karnataka, India","Copyright":"© Amith Nag Photography/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/14.662778,74.278056/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=14.662778,74.278056;S9;Gabit Keni Beach, Ankola, Karnataka, India&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260909_GabitKeni\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Ankola+Karnataka&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260908_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260909_GabitKeni"},"Ssd":"20260909","Name":"GabitKeni","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"6382808847","FullDateString":"9 Sept 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"A beech tree stands alone amid golden fields near East Meon in Hampshire, providing a striking focal point in the rolling landscape of England's South Downs National Park. Agriculture has shaped these chalk hills for centuries, and farming remains an important part of the region today. The area's free-draining chalk soils support extensive arable farming, with wheat and barley among the most common crops. Throughout the summer, these crops ripen in the fields before harvest transforms the countryside into a patchwork of gold and stubble.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.BeechEngland_EN-GB6264734535_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.BeechEngland_EN-GB6264734535_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Fields of gold","Title":"Beech tree in a cereal field, East Meon, South Downs National Park, Hampshire, England","Copyright":"© Guy Edwardes/Minden Pictures","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/50.994476,-1.03351/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=50.994476,-1.03351;S9;East Meon, Hampshire, England&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260908_BeechEngland\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Hampshire+England&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260907_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260908_BeechEngland"},"Ssd":"20260908","Name":"BeechEngland","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"6264734535","FullDateString":"8 Sept 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Perched above the Regnitz River, Bamberg's Old Town Hall is one of Germany's most distinctive landmarks. According to local legend, the town's bishop refused to give citizens land for their town hall, so they created their own artificial island in the river by driving wooden piles into the riverbed. The building that rose there became a symbol of civic independence and remains one of Bavaria's most photographed scenes.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.BambergTownhall_EN-GB6012686407_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.BambergTownhall_EN-GB6012686407_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Where history flows along the canal","Title":"Old Town Hall, Bamberg, Germany","Copyright":"© SCStock/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/49.8942,10.8855/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=49.8942,10.8855;S9;Bamberg, Germany&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260907_BambergTownhall\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Bamberg+Germany&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260906_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260907_BambergTownhall"},"Ssd":"20260907","Name":"BambergTownhall","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"6012686407","FullDateString":"7 Sept 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"At first glance, today's image looks more like a drowned woodland than a lake. Bare tree trunks emerge from the water, their reflections stretching across the surface as the Grampians glow in the distance. This is Lake Fyans, a man-made off-stream reservoir at the foot of the Grampians (Gariwerd) National Park in Victoria, Australia. Part of the regional Wimmera-Mallee water supply system, it also draws anglers with its brown and rainbow trout and trophy-sized redfin.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.LakeFyans_EN-GB5800075953_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.LakeFyans_EN-GB5800075953_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"A reservoir of reflections","Title":"Lake Fyans, Grampians National Park, Victoria, Australia","Copyright":"© tracielouise/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/-37.1431,142.6352/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=-37.1431,142.6352;S9;Lake Fyans, Grampians National Park, Victoria, Australia&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260906_LakeFyans\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Grampians+National+Park+Victoria&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260905_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260906_LakeFyans"},"Ssd":"20260906","Name":"LakeFyans","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"5800075953","FullDateString":"6 Sept 2026"}],"LocStrings":{"LOC_HOMEPAGE_VERTICAL_SCROLL_IOTD":"